{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu8eqGZ6Djo2Y5LznAvY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or wait for the rule to run, so neither has been seen working yet.\n\n**Data:** The logs have a `timestamp` field plus `response` (the status code, stored as a string), `bytes`, `extension`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `clientip`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `referer`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-2b147a37 Web logs overview\" has 5 panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Bytes transferred over time\n- Top source countries (`geo.src`)\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-2b147a37-web-logs-overview-dd977bb3b075.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-2b147a37 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- **Schedule:** it runs every minute.\n- **Condition:** it fires when more than 10 documents with a `response` of 500–599 arrive in a 5-minute window. It matches on `response.keyword` with a regexp, `5[0-9][0-9]`.\n- **State:** the rule was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Actions:** it has no action attached, so it will only record alerts in Kibana and won't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1032,"cache_read_input_tokens":20464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1032},"output_tokens":464,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"cfc139e3-bcec-4d84-84d0-2e50bb96026d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:46:43.265Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu8eq3fRvGAQetEDwL75"}
